<title>USA: Sinter sees Q4 GM strike cost at $0.03/shr.</title>
<headline>Sinter sees Q4 GM strike cost at $0.03/shr.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND, Ohio 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sinter Metals Inc said Monday it lost about $1 million in sales or $0.03 a share in the fourth-quarter as a result of the strikes at General Motors Corp.  </p>
<p>Sinter reported fourth-quarter results of $0.31 a share against $0.27.</p>
<p>U.S. and Canadian auto workers struck GM plants in October and November, while a United Auto Workers strike at two Dayton, Ohio, brake plants crippled the company's North American production.</p>
<p>Sinter makes precision pressed powder metal parts for the automotive, power tool and home appliance industries, among others.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
